cff-version: 1.2.0
type: software
message: >-
  Please cite this software using its Zenodo DOI. The accompanying scientific
  paper's citation can be added once its bibliographic metadata are finalised.
title: "sc_teff_method: K-band Sc I temperature calibration for cool giant stars"
authors:
  - family-names: Thorsbro
    given-names: Brian
version: 1.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23621161
repository-code: "https://github.com/thorsbro/sc_teff_method"
url: "https://github.com/thorsbro/sc_teff_method"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Python implementation of frozen Gaussian and hyperfine-structure (HFS)
  empirical temperature calibrations for nine K-band Sc I lines in cool giant
  stars on the Nandakumar et al. (2023) temperature scale. Each method has
  separate configurations with and without [Fe/H], giving four configurations
  in total. Optional spectral fitting and interactive line review support
  manual continuum adjustment and reproducible saved reviews and outputs.
  The package includes frozen empirical fixed-subset validation statistics
  from the 5 October 2026 nine-line snapshot.
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - stellar effective temperatures
  - scandium
  - cool giant stars
